 Privacy Policy — Cyberpunk Soccer 2099: Striker

**Last updated: [08.08.2026]**

This Privacy Policy explains how Vainsteel Studios handles information in connection with the mobile game Cyberpunk Soccer 2099: Striker. By downloading or playing the Game, you agree to the practices described in this policy.

## Summary
- We do **not** require you to create an account or provide personal details such as your name or email to play.
- Your game progress is stored **locally on your device**.
- We show ads through **Google AdMob**, which may collect device and usage information to serve and measure ads.

## Information We Collect

**Information you provide.** The Game does not ask you to register or submit personal information. If you type a nickname for your in-game profile, it is used only to display your progress [and, where the online leaderboard is enabled, to show your ranking to other players].

**Information stored on your device.** Your career progress, settings, and preferences are saved locally on your device so you can continue playing. We do not have access to this local data.

**Information collected automatically by third parties.** To keep the Game free, we use third-party services (see "Advertising" below) that may automatically collect certain information, such as a device or advertising identifier, IP address, general device information (model, operating system, language), and interactions with ads. This information is collected by those third parties in accordance with their own privacy policies.

## Advertising
We use **Google AdMob** to display advertisements. AdMob may use device identifiers and usage data to serve personalized or non-personalized ads and to measure ad performance. You can learn how Google uses data at https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites and review Google's Privacy Policy at https://policies.google.com/privacy.

**Users in the EEA, the UK, and Switzerland.** Before showing personalized ads, we present a consent request. You can choose to accept personalized ads or continue with non-personalized ads, and you can change your choice later.

## Children's Privacy
The Game is not directed to children under the age of 13 (or the minimum age required in your country), and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has provided us with personal information, please contact us and we will take appropriate steps to address it. Where required, advertising content is configured accordingly.

## Data Retention
Local game data remains on your device until you delete it or uninstall the Game. Data collected by third-party services is retained according to their own policies.

## Your Choices
- **Advertising ID:** You can reset your advertising identifier or opt out of ad personalization in your device settings (Android: Settings › Privacy › Ads).
- **Consent (EEA / UK / Switzerland):** You can withdraw or change your ad consent as described above.
- **Local data:** You can remove all locally stored game data by clearing the app's storage or uninstalling the Game.

## Third-Party Services
The Game relies on the following third-party services, each governed by its own privacy policy:
- **Google AdMob / Google Play Services** — https://policies.google.com/privacy

## Data Security
We take reasonable measures to protect information handled by the Game. However, no method of transmission or electronic storage is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.

## International Users
Because we use global service providers (such as Google), information may be processed and stored in countries other than your own, which may have data protection laws that differ from those in your jurisdiction.

## Changes to This Policy
We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Changes will be posted on this page with a new "Last updated" date. Your continued use of the Game after changes take effect constitutes acceptance of the revised policy.

